    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nIf you are interested in this lovely residence, sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register at SherryFitz.ieSherry FitzGerald Geraghty offer \"Annore House\" to the market, a most spacious family home with generous reception rooms to suit all family members, with garage, a host of features and benefiting from a South/West aspect.Constructed in the 1970's, this lovely home was extended upstairs in the 1990's where 4 double bedrooms are to be had, along with a shower room, en-suite shower room of the main bedroom, a linen closet/walk in wardrobe and access to superb storage in the eaves.The property has been painted internally and externally, has new laminate flooring, new tiled floors in the kitchen and laundry room and newly fitted carpets to the stairs and landing area.Located just off the N2, \"Annore House\" is perfectly positioned for easy access to local Primary Schools, a choice of Secondary Schools in Ashbourne and Ratoath, has easy access to bordering villages, is a short drive to Emerald Theme Park and to all major road networks via the M2 Motorway.Viewing is strictly by prior appointment and for transparency purposes, bidding will be carried out on line via our unique bidding platform: \"MySherryFitz\""
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nTimber front door and glazed side panels, laminae flooring, dado rail, coving, stairs to first floor\n\nSitting Room - \nThis well proportioned room has a feature cast iron fireplace with tiled insert, coving and double doors to dining room\n\nDining Room - \nLaminate flooring, French doors to patio area and garden, coving (double doors to sitting room)\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room - \nStorage cupboards at base and eye level - Birch Timber, providing excellent storage, granite worktops, plumbed for dishwasher, new extractor hood installed, tiled flooring large window and coving, double Georgian style doors to dining room\n\nLaundry Room / Rear Hall - \nThis very spacious laundry room has storage cupboards, a tiled floor, coving, is plumbed for utilities and has an exit door to the patio area and garden\n\nReception Room - \nHaving laminate flooring and coving\n\nBedroom 1 / Study Room - \nLaminate flooring underfoot and coving\n\nWalk in Airing Cupboard - \nInsulated tank, shelving and dual immersion\n\nBathroom - \nBath, WC, WHB, laminate flooring and window for natural light and ventilation\n\nGarage - \nAccess from hallway to garage, having roller shutter door - newly installed, , side window, electrics laid onFuel store to rear with rear exit to gardenGarden Storage Room with access from garage\n\nUpstairs - \nCarpet stairs and landing areaVelux window , access to eaves storage - walk in, flooring and light installedWalk in wardrobe with carpet underfoot (this area is positioned over the downstairs bathroom - possible potential en-suite to adjacent bedroom\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble bedroom with laminate flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 - \nDouble bedroom with laminate flooring, built in wardrobes and coving\n\nBedroom 4 - \nAnother double bedroom with laminate flooring, built in wardrobes and coving\n\nMain Bedroom - \nHaving built in wardrobes and laminate flooring. Fold away stair access to attic space (insulated)\n\nEn-Suite Shower Room - \nTiled shower, tiled floor, electric wall radiator - trimer in attic, window for natural light and ventilation\n\nBathroom / Shower Room - \nElectric shower, tiled floor, towel radiator and Velux window for natural light and ventilation\n\nExterior - \nBeautifully kept gardens and hedging with mature trees - some crab apple trees to rearBoiler House, oil tank, outdoor tap, (original septic tank - positioned mid-way in rear garden)\n\nIncluded in Sale - \nWindow dressings, carpets, light fixtures & fittings, extractor hood\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>South/West facing to rear</li><li>Constructed 1970's, extended 1990's to 2 story - for upstairs bedrooms</li><li>Freshly painted - inside and out</li><li>New carpets and laminate flooring, kitchen and laundry room tiled</li><li>Windows replaced in 1997</li><li>New roller shutter door to garage</li><li>Chimney cleaned and vacuumed 4 years ago, spinner on top of chimney</li><li>Large walk in storage in eaves, floored and light installed</li><li>Large laundry room - rear exit</li><li>Very spacious storage area in eaves - floored, light installed</li><li>Key box at front wall </li><li>Short drive to local schools at Cushenstown, Curraha, Rathfeigh and Ashbourne</li><li>Short drive to Emerald Park Theme park</li><li>Easy access neighbouring villages and Ashbourne town and all major access routes via M2</li><li>Mains Services, drainage by septic tank - original tank, OFCH - boiler replaced 10 years ago - recently serviced, outdoor tap</ul>"
      },
